<title>BELGIUM: New Zealand to restrain sheepmeat exports to EU.</title>
<headline>New Zealand to restrain sheepmeat exports to EU.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand has pledged restraint over rising exports of sheepmeat to the European Union, Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler told agriculture ministers on Monday.</p>
<p>A Commission official said on Tuesday imports of chilled sheepmeat from New Zealand had risen to 16,000 tonnes between 1994 and 1996 from 9,200 tonnes. France has said a further 25,000 tonnes was expected in 1997.</p>
<p>Replying to a French demand for restrictions on chilled sheepmeat imports, Fischler said that no distinction could be drawn between chilled and frozen meat, the official said.</p>
<p>Fischler reported that New Zealand had given the Commission an assurance it would exercise restraint, particularly during sensitive periods such as Christmas and Easter. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
